
GRASP case1_mpi calculation scripts

This example uses 34 MPI processes on one Kaya node.

The MPI process count is obtained from the SLURM allocation
through the SLURM_NTASKS environment variable.

The main calculation workflow is:

1. sh_files_c  - Generate the configuration state functions
2. sh_nuc      - Obtain nuclear data
3. sh_initial  - Generate initial wavefunction estimates
4. sh_scf      - Perform self-consistent-field and CI calculations
5. sh_tr       - Perform transition calculations

The main script sh_case1 runs these steps in sequence.

The MPI process count is controlled by grasp_mpi.slurm.
Do not change the process count independently in these scripts.
